    "body": "Picture a festival tent: fiddle and flute launch a reel; whistle joins in unison; pipes sit out until a slow air set; harp opens a concert earlier in the day. Picture a kitchen: whistle learner practises cuts while a piper tunes regulators on the sofa. None of these instruments owns a fixed slot labelled \"melody\" — pipes harmonise, fiddle drives rhythm, harp accompanies song.\n\nYour homework is ear training: pick one recording each from Coleman, Molloy, Bergin, O'Flynn, and Kelly (or Carroll, Hayes, Madden, Clancy, Ní Chathasaigh). Note ornament density, tempo, and space between phrases. Bring that listening to Session Voices II, where guitar, accordion, and bodhrán complete the ensemble picture.\n\nPicture a festival tent: fiddle and flute launch a reel; whistle joins in unison; pipes sit out until a slow air set; harp opens a concert earlier in the day. Picture a kitchen: whistle learner practises cuts while a piper tunes regulators on the sofa. None of these instruments owns a fixed slot labelled \"melody\" — pipes harmonise, fiddle drives rhythm, harp accompanies song.\n\nYour homework is ear training: pick one recording each from Coleman, Molloy, Bergin, O'Flynn, and Kelly (or Carroll, Hayes, Madden, Clancy, Ní Chathasaigh). Note ornament density, tempo, and space between phrases. Bring that listening to Session Voices II, where guitar, accordion, and bodhrán complete the ensemble picture.",
