    "body": "Experienced session players run a mental checklist in the first eight bars of any tune:\n\n1. Metre — reel, double jig, slip jig, hornpipe, polka, slide, or something rarer?\n2. Mode and key — D major, E minor, A mixolydian flavour?\n3. Regional accent — Sligo rolls, Donegal snap, Clare box phrasing?\n4. Set position — is this the opening tune or the third reel in a chain?\n\nYou do not need perfect pitch to participate; you need pattern recognition. Apps like The Session and tune databases in ABC notation help once you know the form. ABC is a text format musicians share online — one line of letters and numbers can encode a whole reel. Treat ABC as a map back to recordings, not a substitute for listening.\n\nWhen someone starts a tune you almost know, wait one repetition before joining. Trad etiquette favours the listener who enters cleanly over the enthusiast who guesses wrong and drags the room off pulse.\n\nExperienced session players run a mental checklist in the first eight bars of any tune: 1. Metre — reel, double jig, slip jig, hornpipe, polka, slide, or something rarer? 2. Mode and key — D major, E minor, A mixolydian flavour? 3. Regional accent — Sligo rolls, Donegal snap, Clare box phrasing? 4. Set position — is this the opening tune or the third reel in a chain? You do not need perfect pitch to participate; you need pattern recognition. Apps like The Session and tune databases in ABC notation help once you know the form. ABC is a text format musicians share online — one line of letters and numbers can encode a whole reel. Treat ABC as a…",
