    "body": "Accounts from folklore collectors describe curricula that mixed etiquette and athletics: where to stand in a kitchen set, how to honour the musician, how to recover from a missed step without stopping the figure. Masters sometimes settled disputes between families over who danced first — dance was social power, not only entertainment.\n\nRivals competed for pupils; legends tell of dance-offs on table tops and wagers on who could execute the most complex treble. Whether every story is literal truth matters less than what they reveal: dance mastery was public reputation, like fiddle virtuosity today.\n\nAccounts from folklore collectors describe curricula that mixed etiquette and athletics: where to stand in a kitchen set, how to honour the musician, how to recover from a missed step without stopping the figure. Masters sometimes settled disputes between families over who danced first — dance was social power, not only entertainment.\n\nRivals competed for pupils; legends tell of dance-offs on table tops and wagers on who could execute the most complex treble. Whether every story is literal truth matters less than what they reveal: dance mastery was public reputation, like fiddle virtuosity today.",
