    "body": "Irish dance today is not one style but a family of traditions:\n\n| Tradition | Scale | Footwork | Typical music |\n|-----------|-------|----------|---------------|\n| Céilí | Groups, choreographed figures | Moderate | Reels, jigs; céilí bands |\n| Set dancing | Four couples per set, quadrille heritage | Moderate, figure-driven | Reels, jigs, polkas, slides |\n| Step dance | Solo (or line spectacle) | Rapid, codified | Reels, jigs, hornpipes, slip jigs |\n| Sean-nós dance | Solo, improvisatory | Low, percussive | Sean-nós song, free rhythm |\n\nThese overlap in musicians' lives — the same fiddler may play for a céilí, a set, and a pub session on one weekend — but each tradition asks different questions about tempo, phrasing, and who leads (caller, adjudicator, or singer).\n\nIrish dance today is not one style but a family of traditions: | Tradition | Scale | Footwork | Typical music | |-----------|-------|----------|---------------| | Céilí | Groups, choreographed figures | Moderate | Reels, jigs; céilí bands | | Set dancing | Four couples per set, quadrille heritage | Moderate, figure-driven | Reels, jigs, polkas, slides | | Step dance | Solo (or line spectacle) | Rapid, codified | Reels, jigs, hornpipes, slip jigs | | Sean-nós dance | Solo, improvisatory | Low, percussive | Sean-nós song, free rhythm | These overlap in musicians' lives — the same fiddler may play for a céilí, a set, and a pub session on one weekend — but each tradition asks different questions about…",
