    "body": "Riverdance premiered as the Eurovision 1994 interval act in Dublin — Jean Butler, Michael Flatley, Anúna, and Whelan's score. The seven-minute act drew a standing ovation; the stage show opened at the Gaiety Theatre on 9 February 1995 and toured for decades, reshaping global perception of Irish music and dance.\n\nRiverdance is theatre: orchestral arrangement, lighting, linear choreography, unified arm lines. It is not a pub session or a kitchen set. Critics sometimes mourn what spectacle omits; historians note what it funded — millions of children in dance classes, renewed interest in trad, and a new economic layer around Irish culture.\n\nRiverdance premiered as the Eurovision 1994 interval act in Dublin — Jean Butler, Michael Flatley, Anúna, and Whelan's score. The seven-minute act drew a standing ovation; the stage show opened at the Gaiety Theatre on 9 February 1995 and toured for decades, reshaping global perception of Irish music and dance.\n\nRiverdance is theatre: orchestral arrangement, lighting, linear choreography, unified arm lines. It is not a pub session or a kitchen set. Critics sometimes mourn what spectacle omits; historians note what it funded — millions of children in dance classes, renewed interest in trad, and a new economic layer around Irish culture.",
