    "body": "Oireachtas na Gaeilge (annual festival of Irish culture) centres Irish language — sean-nós song, scéalaíocht (storytelling), agallamh beirte (dialogue verse), and dance traditions aligned with festival aesthetics. It is not interchangeable with Fleadh Cheoil though some artists appear in both.\n\nMusicians backing Oireachtas competitions learn song-first logic similar to sean-nós dance: the amhrán sets timing; instruments enter sparingly if at all. English-language ballad stages at folk festivals operate differently — chorus participation, guitar accompaniment, louder PA.\n\nRespecting this distinction marks you as culturally literate in mixed Irish arts spaces.\n\nOireachtas na Gaeilge (annual festival of Irish culture) centres Irish language — sean-nós song, scéalaíocht (storytelling), agallamh beirte (dialogue verse), and dance traditions aligned with festival aesthetics. It is not interchangeable with Fleadh Cheoil though some artists appear in both.\n\nMusicians backing Oireachtas competitions learn song-first logic similar to sean-nós dance: the amhrán sets timing; instruments enter sparingly if at all. English-language ballad stages at folk festivals operate differently — chorus participation, guitar accompaniment, louder PA.\n\nRespecting this distinction marks you as culturally literate in mixed Irish arts spaces.",
